<h2>Xenia claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Why do so many Xenia homes date from the 1970s?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The April 3, 1974 tornado destroyed a large share of the city, and much of it was rebuilt over the following years. Those homes are now about fifty years old, which affects depreciation and repair decisions in claims.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Beavercreek fall within your Xenia service area?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We work throughout Greene County, including Beavercreek, Fairborn, Bellbrook, Yellow Springs, Cedarville and Wilberforce, as well as the surrounding Miami Valley.</p></div></details><details><summary>How can I recover depreciation withheld on my Greene County roof claim?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many replacement-cost policies pay actual cash value first and release the withheld depreciation after repairs are completed. Check your policy for the deadline to complete repairs and submit proof, and keep all invoices.</p></div></details></div>
